@* Arabic, and written in Arabic: the labels are translated and the page numbers are Arabic-Indic
   digits, because a mirrored English row is a direction rather than a translation.

   Nothing rotates the chevrons here. They carry rtl:rotate-180 already, so "previous" points the
   way the reader came from — which is the one thing a mirrored pagination usually gets wrong, and
   rotating them again at the call site is how it gets got wrong twice. *@
<div dir="rtl">
    <Pagination>
        <PaginationContent>
            <PaginationItem>
                <PaginationPrevious Href="/components/pagination?page=1" Label="السابق"
                                    AriaLabel="الصفحة السابقة" />
            </PaginationItem>
            <PaginationItem><PaginationLink Href="/components/pagination?page=1">١</PaginationLink></PaginationItem>
            <PaginationItem><PaginationLink Href="/components/pagination?page=2" IsActive>٢</PaginationLink></PaginationItem>
            <PaginationItem><PaginationLink Href="/components/pagination?page=3">٣</PaginationLink></PaginationItem>
            <PaginationItem><PaginationEllipsis SrLabel="صفحات أخرى" /></PaginationItem>
            <PaginationItem>
                <PaginationNext Href="/components/pagination?page=3" Label="التالي"
                                AriaLabel="الصفحة التالية" />
            </PaginationItem>
        </PaginationContent>
    </Pagination>
</div>
